    "Pressed note transparency (%)": "Hit note transparency",
    "ColorHelp": "Write R, G and B from 0 to 255; a blank box counts as 0. These colors belong to the note area only and are separate from the window theme. The judgment line color is also used for the hit glow. Changing a color keeps the notes and the clock as they are.",
    "Experimental features": "Experimental features",
    "ExperimentalHelp": "Shows the experimental card below. It holds rules still being tried out; while this is off, experimental settings keep their values and change nothing.",
    "ExperimentalSectionHelp": "Rules that are still being tried out. If you do not like them, turn Experimental features off in Advanced to go back.",
    "ExperimentalNone": "This version has no experimental features.",
    "Chord lane preference": "Chord lane preference",
    "No chord center pair": "No chords across the center",
    "NoChordCenterHelp": "On (default): on four lanes a chord never uses the pair across the center (lanes 2-3), only 1-2 or 3-4. Off: 2-3 may be used too, though another pair is still used first whenever the block fits there.",
    "ChordLaneHelp": "Which pair a chord takes first: 1-2 is the left hand, 3-4 the right. None (default) follows the pattern order. A taken pair, or one held by a long note, still sends the chord elsewhere. Singles are placed the same either way.",
    "ChordLaneNone": "None",
    "Trill window (ms)": "Trill window (ms)",
    "No trill center pair": "No trill center pair",
    "Trill lane preference": "Trill lane preference",
    "TrillHelp": "Two single notes this close are a trill and share one pair of lanes, so they can be played with two fingers. Chords are grouped first, so the chord window wins; 0 switches trills off. They are not colored differently.",
    "NoTrillCenterHelp": "Keeps a trill off the pair that crosses the screen center (lanes 2-3) on four lanes, as the chord setting does.",
    "TrillLaneHelp": "Which pair a trill takes first; the same choices and default as the chord lane preference.",
    "Hint.TrillWindowMs": "How close two single notes have to be to read as a trill.",
    "Hint.NoTrillCenterPair": "Keeps trills off the center pair on four lanes.",
    "Hint.TrillLanePreference": "Which pair a trill takes first.",
    "Error.TrillWindow": "The trill window must be between 0 and 200 ms. 0 switches trills off.",
    "Error.TrillLane": "The trill lane preference must be None, 1-2, 3-4 or 1-2,3-4.",
    "SectionMagic": "Magic circle",
    "Magic circle max interval (ms)": "Max interval (ms)",
    "MagicCircleIntervalHelp": "Runs slower than this are not magic circles. With 100, a run of notes 100ms or more apart never counts, however long it is.",
    "Judgment line fade in (ms)": "Bar fade in (ms)",
    "Judgment line fade out (ms)": "Bar fade out (ms)",
    "MagicCircleFadeHelp": "How long the bar takes to appear and to disappear. Fade in runs while it rises, fade out after the run ends. 0 shows and hides it at once.",
    "Fixed tiles": "Fixed tiles",
    "MagicCircleFixedHelp": "On: the tile count is held at the value below through a magic circle. Entering one switches at once instead of waiting for the cycle, and the dynamic count returns when the run ends. This changes where notes are placed.",
    "Fixed tile count": "Fixed tile count",
    "MagicCircleTilesHelp": "The tile count used through a magic circle. It can never exceed the maximum tile count and leaves the list when the maximum drops below it.",
    "Checkpoint color": "Checkpoint note",
    "Start note color": "Start note",
    "End note color": "End note",
    "Hint.ChordLanePreference": "Which lane pair a chord takes first",
    "Hint.NoChordCenterPair": "Keeps chords off lanes 2-3 on four lanes",
    "Hint.MagicCircleMaxIntervalMs": "Runs slower than this are not magic circles",
    "Hint.MagicCircleFadeInMs": "How long the bar takes to appear",
    "Hint.MagicCircleFadeOutMs": "How long the bar takes to disappear",
    "Hint.MagicCircleFixedTiles": "Holds the tile count through a magic circle",
    "Hint.MagicCircleTileCount": "The tile count used through a magic circle",
    "Hint.CheckpointColor": "Color of a note on a checkpoint tile",
    "Hint.StartNoteColor": "Color of the first note of each play; it outranks every other note color",
    "Hint.EndNoteColor": "Color of the song's last note; it outranks every color but the start note",
    "Chord section lanes": "Chord section lanes",
    "ChordLanesHelp": "On: the singles right after a chord keep its two lanes free and use the others instead (1-2 3 2 3 becomes 1-2 3 4 3). The rule ends once two cycles (4 groups on 2 lanes, 8 on 4) pass without a chord. The chord's own lanes and the notes before it are unchanged, and the rule is relaxed step by step when too few lanes are left.",
    "Extra lanes": "Extra lane placement",
    "ExtraLanesHelp": "Adds one lane on each side of a 2-, 4- or 6-lane view (two on the other side when the pattern uses tile 1 or 8). They stay empty except for the notes of a chord group that cannot be placed otherwise, which come down there as singles. Songs that can be placed keep the same notes.",
    "ExtraLanesUnavailable": "Not used now: the maximum is 1 or 8 lanes, or no free tile is left beside the pattern. The switch keeps its value.",
    "Judgment slowdown": "Judgment line slowdown",
    "JudgmentSlowdownHelp": "On: a note past the judgment line takes the press window to reach the bottom line and vanishes when the window ends. Off: unpressed notes vanish the moment their window ends and pressed ones keep travelling. Display only, so the notes are not prepared again.",
    "Magic circle judgment line": "Magic circle timing bar",
    "MagicCircleHelp": "In a run of equal intervals (a magic circle) a bar in the middle of the lanes shows whether recent presses were early or late: left is early, right is late, and the ends are the press window. Switching it off locks every other row on this card.",
    "Magic circle notes": "Magic circle note count",
    "MagicCircleNotesHelp": "A run of this many notes with the same interval (±5ms of the first one) counts as a magic circle. Chords share a display time and count once. Raising it ignores short bursts and keeps only long runs.",
    "Magic circle lead (ms)": "Judgment line lead (ms)",
    "MagicCircleLeadHelp": "Shows the bar this long before the run starts so the eye can settle first. How long it takes to rise is the fade in above.",
    "MagicCircleFast": "Early",
    "MagicCircleSlow": "Late",
    "Tile preference toggle": "Tile preference",
    "Keep speed on load": "Keep the loaded speed",
    "Pause aligns next note": "Paused note position",
    "KeepSpeedHelp": "On: loading a song keeps the playback speed. Off (default): every load puts the speed back to 100%; that counts as a settings change and can be rolled back.",
    "PauseAlignHelp": "Escape or the pause button puts the next note you have not pressed on the judgment line, as the game resumes on the tile it stopped at. Off, the notes stay where the pause caught them.",
    "TilePreferenceToggleHelp": "Off: every pattern cycles from the highest tile down (3 4 5 6 becomes 6 5 4 3). On: each mode follows the order written beside it. Turning it off keeps the written orders for later.",
    "TilePreferenceHelp": "Ranks the pattern tiles by number, 1 being the lowest. Tiles 3 4 5 6 with the order 4 3 2 1 cycle as 6 5 4 3. It only applies while the tile preference is on in Advanced.",
    "PatternTilesHelp": "The tile numbers (1-8) this mode uses, separated by spaces. The order does not matter and is sorted on Apply; the cycle order comes from the preference beside it. Tiles outside the maximum pattern are not on screen and are rejected.",
    "1K pattern · Initial tile": "1K pattern · initial tile",
    "InitialTileHelp": "The tile used through 1-lane sections and the one the first cycle starts on after a reset. Starting from a checkpoint or a section cuts the full-song placement instead, so it does not apply there.",
    "MapFolderHelp": "The folder map sync reads. It walks subfolders for .adofai files and only ever reads them. The file button beside it fills in a path without opening or writing anything.",
    "DataFolderHelp": "The app-owned folder that holds the settings and the song cache. Leave it empty for the default location every copy of the app on this PC shares (%LOCALAPPDATA%/AdofaiVisualizer). A path that is the map folder, or inside it, is rejected. Changing it never moves or deletes the old files, so songs have to be synced again in the new folder.",
