    "ResetLoaded": "Loaded the defaults into the form. Press Apply below to confirm.",
    "Help": "Guide",
    "HelpBody": "Getting started\nType a song title in the song box or pick one, then press Load. Loading while the visualizer is off turns it on, and the song · checkpoint panel folds afterwards. The ◀ ▶ beside the song box load the previous or next song and wrap around at the ends of the list. First, Sync reads the songs of the map folder (setting → Advanced, default: Steam Workshop). Example (Plum - R) works without syncing. Map files are only read.\n\nPlaying with the game\nPress the start key ({1}) as you hit the first tile in the game; notes leave the judgment line. Reset ({0}) prepares the chosen position again. With the global input scope on, keys react only while ADOFAI or this visualizer is focused. Game input is never blocked. While stopped, the middle of the note field shows the song title, song info, start point, song length and tile count.\n\nLane keys\n{3} map to tiles 1–8 (the default 4-lane view uses the middle four). Pressing lights the lane and fades the note near the judgment line; a note left unpressed disappears when its press window ends and turns its lane red. Hold a long note and let go at its end; letting go too early counts as missed. This is practice feedback, not the game's judgment or score.\n\nCalibration and magic circles\nAfter the start, the first few presses (Timing → calibration notes) are averaged and the display is shifted once. Turn on the magic circle timing bar in Advanced to get a bar in the middle of the lanes during long runs of one interval, showing whether presses are early (left) or late (right).\n\nCheckpoints and sections\nPick a checkpoint from the list or with {5} (next) / {4} (previous). Type a game tile number in the section box to prepare from just after that tile. Starting from a checkpoint or a section keeps the lanes of a full play, and the first note's lane key becomes the start key. With Auto on, the checkpoint follows as soon as its note is pressed (or when its press window ends). At a speed other than 100% or from a section, auto is off, as in the game.\n\nPause (Esc)\nEsc in the game also pauses the notes. After resuming the game and its countdown, press the next tile: the note of that lane within 1 second of the pause is put on the judgment line and play continues.\n\nNote shapes\nSky blue is a single note, green is a two-lane chord, and a long bar is a long note. Three or more simultaneous notes are shown as chords and a single. If chords cannot be placed, you are asked whether to enable extra lane placement, and if that does not help, whether to raise the maximum tile count.\n\nsetting\nChange general options (language, guide buttons, song info, global input scope), controls, visualization (travel time, scales, judgment line, effects), design (colors and transparency), timing (speed, chords, waits, calibration, magic circles) and lanes and patterns. Pick the theme at the top right. Blank fields return to defaults, and ★ marks changes not applied yet. Advanced holds extra lane placement, the judgment line slowdown, tile preference, the magic circle bar, the map folder and JSON export, import and reset. Settings reset when the app closes (to DefaultSettings.jsonc), so keep them as JSON.\n\nEditing a song\nOpen it with Edit song in the settings or edit in the console. Only lanes and chord grouping change; timing and judgment stay. Pick with click or drag (Ctrl for one, Shift for a range), move lanes with a/d or numbers, step with w/s. m merges, u splits, Ctrl+Z undoes, Ctrl+Shift+Z redoes, Ctrl+wheel zooms. Saving fills one of the song's nine slots, shown in the list as 2*.",
