    "UpdateNotesClose": "OK",
    "ReleaseNotes.1.0.1": "· Note placement reads better: the same key no longer comes twice in a row where it can be avoided (3 3 2 3 2, 3-4 3-4), and a single between chords sits right beside them (2 3-4 2 3-4).\n· Trills follow the pattern's direction: on a 4-3-2-1 pattern they read 4-3 and 2-1, two trills in a row take two pairs, and the note after a trill sits right beside it (3 after 1-2).\n· The first and last notes are a deep yellow by default. Colors you already changed stay as they are.\n· Hide on the song details now folds away the controls and the dark band too, leaving only a Show button.\n· The song box always takes typing; the search switch is gone from the settings.\n· The song editor keeps its tools beside the sheet: every shortcut has a button, and the zoom shows in percent with a reset.\n· The console has pin, unpin and go: pin the tiles you practise and pick them with Tab after go. An original and its edits share their pins.\n· The linker (the game link mod) comes with the app, so the console's install linker puts it in place on its own.",
    "ReleaseNotes.1.0.0": "· The first full release.\n· The app has its own icon.\n· The first note of each play and the song's last note have their own colors, shown over the checkpoint color. Change them in Settings > Colors.\n· A second after a song ends, it offers to play again. The reset key (Enter by default) closes the offer and goes back to the last checkpoint, or to the beginning when there is none or checkpoints are not automatic.\n· A song that starts on a chord no longer shows one half of it pressed as play starts.\n· Songs and settings are kept in one place on this PC, so the app shows the same song list and settings wherever it runs from.",
